Seed: a CompareTo that is projected rather than compared is left to EF Core's CASE, which is NULL for a null operand
Oracles: RangeOrderParityTests
Fails: Select(r => r.Seats.CompareTo(none)) with none null throws on materialization ("Nullable object must have a value") where Comparer<T>.Default answers 1
History: found by the final pre-release analysis (#253) before 10.0.0 shipped

